WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:07.339
Take a dash of ET, add a pinch of Despicable
Me, Lilo &amp; Stitch, Madagascar, Toy Story,

00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:13.050
and a drop of Star Wars, and you get DreamWorks’
colourful and cute animated feature, Home!

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:18.290
Adapted from Adam Rex’s children’s book,
The True Meaning Of Smekday, Home is an odd

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:22.250
couple, culture clash, alien-invasion, road
trip, buddy comedy!

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:27.199
Basically, the film follows what happens when
a cowardly alien race called the Boov head

00:00:27.199 --> 00:00:30.750
to Earth to escape their equally alien enemy
the Gorg.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:36.190
Once on our planet, the Boovs take it over,
relocating all human beings to Australia.

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:41.219
But when an unconventional Boov called Oh
accidentally lets their arch-nemesis know

00:00:41.219 --> 00:00:46.219
where they’re hiding, he finds himself on
the run and ends up forming an unlikely friendship

00:00:46.219 --> 00:00:49.839
with a young girl called Tip who’s looking
for her relocated mother.

00:00:49.839 --> 00:00:54.479
Home doesn’t exactly break new ground, and
while it’s no How To Train Your Dragon or

00:00:54.479 --> 00:00:58.370
Shrek, there is still lots to like about DreamWorks’
latest feature.

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:03.579
There’s plenty of zany comedy, much of which
stems from the Boovs’ rather unique uses

00:01:03.579 --> 00:01:08.289
for our earthling products which they’ve
never seen before, including hairdryers,

00:01:08.289 --> 00:01:14.030
vacuums, oranges, barbecues, and bubble wrap.
The animation itself is bright and colourful,

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:18.229
and will doubtless appeal to kids, and the
overall feel of the movie is fun, and I found

00:01:18.229 --> 00:01:23.320
myself laughing quite a bit, though it does
get a touch saccharine towards the end.

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:26.200
There’s also some great voice acting from
the leads.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:31.450
But, as with Neill Blomkamp’s robot movie
Chappie, how much you enjoy Home will really

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:35.759
depend on whether you warm to the central
character, Oh, who’s voiced by actor Jim

00:01:35.759 --> 00:01:40.090
Parsons, best known for playing Sheldon Cooper
in The Big Bang Theory.

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:44.499
The Boov speak in fractured English that has
an intriguing take on our grammar.

00:01:44.499 --> 00:01:49.899
For example, Oh says stuff like “You have
in nick time saved us”, and “Can I come

00:01:49.899 --> 00:01:54.070
into the out now?” when he wants Tip to
let him out of the fridge she locks him in

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:58.999
when they first meet.
Personally, I thought Jim Parsons’ Sheldon-meets-Yoda-style

00:01:58.999 --> 00:02:01.219
performance was pretty engaging.

00:02:01.219 --> 00:02:05.950
Pop star Rihanna makes her animated feature
debut as the voice of 12-year-old Tip, and

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:09.460
she invests the character with refreshing
vitality and warmth.

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:13.080
But Rihanna’s role as Tip isn’t the singer’s
only part in the movie.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:18.440
Her music also makes several appearances on
the soundtrack; as does a song by her on-screen

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:22.220
mother Jennifer Lopez.
Although the tracks are pretty catchy, the

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:26.450
number of them does kinda make it feel like
the movie was made to sell Rihanna’s album.

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:31.360
Tip’s cat, which is called Pig, makes a
cute addition to their little team of two,

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:36.470
even if it does remind me of Tadashi and Hiro’s
cat from Big Hero 6.

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:41.800
And as head Boov, Captain Smek, Steve Martin
brings some animated fun to the proceedings.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:46.880
We’ve seen the movie’s message about friendship
and individuality many times before in similar

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:51.370
fare, though Home does throw in something
a little different with the idea that the

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:56.060
Boovs who view themselves as the liberators
and friends of the humans they’ve invaded,

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:58.800
are actually seen as quite the opposite by
the earthlings.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:04.080
So, to sum up: Though Home won’t stay with
you as long as the Toy Storys and Shreks of

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:09.360
the animated world, it is a sweet, colourful
treat that will keep you and the kids entertained

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:13.790
for 90 minutes.
Home gets 3 out of 5 Flicks.

